    "Region registry (PROJECT_BRIEF.md 4.1). Read by the Python pipeline and, unchanged, by the client.",
    "Coordinates are decimal degrees, WGS84, west longitudes negative. Distances are km.",
    "A REGION is one domain: one model data crop (bbox), fetched once, and one north-up 3D scene covering that crop. It holds the models, stations and zone forecasts.",
    "A SUBAREA is a named part of a region's water. The camera jumps to it and summaries are computed over it. 'box' is its water box, taken from the matching briefing site so the two sites agree.",
    "A subarea MAY have an 'axis' when channelled flow makes along/across cross-sections meaningful. Its origin is the throat midpoint; +along points toward downstreamBearingDeg and +across to the right of downstream. 'viewBox' is its channel-aligned close-up, in along/across km.",
    "axis.* values come from pipeline/geometry/strait_axis.py. Check them with python -m pipeline.regions (it re-measures and fails on drift). Don't edit them by hand.",
    "Stations: 'source' records where each coordinate came from; 'approx' means it was rounded at the source. Radar sites are listed for VAD wind profiles only. This project has no radar visualization."
